// OWNER: UX-24
//
// The Filters & LUT panel (ux.md §10.7, ARCH §6.5, §10.2): the Filters tool's panel for one picture
// clip.
//
// * **Looks:** a horizontal carousel of "None" and the 12 built-in looks (`assets/looks/<id>.vlut`,
//   generated by tool/gen_looks.dart). Each tile shows a still the engine rendered for the clip at the
//   playhead with that look (`PreviewSession.renderLookStills`), or a gradient swatch until it
//   arrives (and when the engine cannot render one). Tapping a tile applies `SetLook` (one history
//   entry); the intensity of the previous look is kept. The Intensity row (0-100 %, not keyframable)
//   shows while a look is applied and writes `look.intensity` through `InspectorPropertyRow`.
// * **My LUTs:** "Import .cube" asks the system picker for a `.cube` file, parses it in
//   `Isolate.run` (CORE-21) so a bad file is explained with its line ("This LUT couldn't be read
//   (line 14: expected 3 numbers)."), then hands it to the media pool service (CORE-27), which writes
//   the project-owned `.cube` and `.vlut` and returns the asset; the panel applies it as the clip's
//   look. Imported LUTs appear as tiles; a long press (or the semantics actions) offers Rename and
//   Remove from project (which first clears the look from the clips that use it).
// * The header's reset removes the look.
// * The thumbnails are best effort: no engine, no preview session or any render failure leaves the
//   swatches, never an error.

